<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Oct 29.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Oct 29.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF OCTOBER 29 VERSUS OCTOBER 22, 1996	     DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA   19/22    1/0     252/260   81/728  353/354    191</p>
<p> SASK.	0/2     0/0	72/66     4/5     76/73	42</p>
<p> B.C.	 0/0     0/0	19/20    17/18    36/38	 9</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 2/2	2/2	4/4	  0</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 2/2	0/0	2/2	  1</p>
<p> TOTAL     19/24    1/0     347/350  104/971  471/471    243</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>-- Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624</p>
